A||||6||DJRice||Replacing Deck Lid Fiero Label||||5||
Z||000000||DJRice||12-08-1999||09:18 AM||||Well Ive had my '87 for almost a a year and a half now and the one thing its missing is the "Fiero" on the Deck Lid.  Apparently, whoever repainted the car didnt bother replacing the sticker.  I recently ordered the rebush kit for my dog bone (I snatched and old one from an 85) from the Fiero Store and thought that would be a good time to go ahead and order the replacement sticker.  Well, It didnt come with any application instructions, and I dont want to ruin a $10 sticker so my question is How do I put this thing on?<P><BR>Also, What kind of HP increase can I expect? <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Had to ask  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||fierospeeder||12-08-1999||12:07 PM||||i know you want to use something like window cleaner on the surface and a papertowel to get all the grease off.  Im not sure about applying it.  I know theres the sticker that you apply water to it and squeege the air bubbles out of it.  Maybe later in the day someone knows that real answer.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Wolfhound||12-08-1999||12:22 PM||||If the Decal is like the custom vinyl names I've used on boats it has a front and rear paper backing.<BR>You clean the surface good (degrease) and wet the area you want to apply it to with a mild solution on dishwashing liquid. Remove the rear backing and apply. The dishwashing solution allows you to slide it around and position it with out it sticking the first place it touches. You then squeege the solution out, then pull the paper off the front very carfully and you have it.<BR>Coy||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||12-08-1999||04:04 PM||||Are you asking how to physically attach the sticker or exactly where to locate it?<P>I got a new intake plenum sticker from Rodney Dickman.  It has adhesive backing and is on a clear background.  I simply peeled off the cardboard backing snd placed it on the intake.  If yours is the same I only caution you not to touch the glue on the backing because it will probably show your fingerprints.<P>Where did you get the sticker?<P>Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Gokart||12-08-1999||09:02 PM||||I got my deck lid decal from Rodney Dickman and I just went over the area with OOOPS first. It removes everything except the paint unless it's latex)! His decal says Fiero GT!||||reg||1
Z||000005||DJRice||12-09-1999||09:23 AM||||I got mine from the Fiero Store, and It goes on the Deck Lid.  I was just curious how to prep the area and put the sticker on.  It has a thin white paper strip on the front and a thicker brown colored paper on the back of it.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||RZURCTN||12-09-1999||09:51 AM||||Definitely clean the area well.  make sure it is dry and lint-free.  Use a piece of masking tape and tape along the top edge of the sticker with about an inch of overhang.  This will allow you to get the sticker perfectly aligned before you take off the back.  Get it aligned where you want it, make sure that the masking tape is stuck down good, then flip the sticker up.  Peel off the backing and slowly lay it down from top to bottom.  make sure you get all the air bubble out.  Doing it this way will minimize your chance of getting air bubble in it.  You can also use something like a small plastic 'Bondo board' to "squeegee" the sticker on.   Once you get it al stuck down, go over it again to make sure it is well seated and sealed.  then peel off the masking tape and the cover tape and WALLA!  You're Done!  Hope this helps!<P>Oh yeah!...you should also notice anywhere from a 5 to 10 hp increase and a definite rise in "Cool" factor!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by RZURCTN (edited 12-09-1999).]||||reg||1
